# Off-machine pair: the USB disk's Backup folder to a NAS, once a day.
# Copy to mirrors-nas.conf (gitignored) and set your own paths.
# /Volumes/Offsite is a NAS share mounted over SMB; it is the only
# destination here not on this Mac, so it is the copy that survives theft,
# fire or a dead Mac.
#
# Format matches mirrors.conf. Run this list ADDITIVE (MIRROR_SYNC_ADDITIVE=1):
# the NAS Backup folder may already hold history the USB disk does not have,
# such as older sd-db snapshots in sd-backups/. An exact mirror would delete
# that history on its first pass.
#
# /Volumes/local/Backup carries the nightly sd-db snapshot in sd-backups/,
# so this pair is also how that snapshot leaves the machine.
/Volumes/local/Backup|/Volumes/Offsite/Backup
